  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "As of January 23, 2025, Micheál Martin is the Taoiseach (Prime Minister) of Ireland. Leader of the Fianna Fáil party, he previously held this office from 2020 to 2022 and currently leads the government following an agreement between Fianna Fáil, Fine Gael, and independent TDs, succeeding Simon Harris. Key Details regarding the Taoiseach: Definition: The Taoiseach (pronounced tee-shock) is the head of government of Ireland. Current Incumbent: Micheál Martin. Role: He leads the cabinet, shapes government policy, and is appointed by the President after nomination by the Dáil Éireann (Irish Parliament). Recent Activity: As of March 2026, Micheál Martin has been conducting official duties, including the traditional St. Patrick's Day visit to Washington, D.C.. The office was established by the 1937 Constitution of Ireland, replacing the previous title of President of the Executive Council.",
